Motion is filed pursuant to LBR\nL31@P0: 9013-1(q), which provides for granting of motions without a hearing. The full Motion is attached, including\nL32@P0: the legal and factual grounds upon which the Motion is made.\nL33@P0: This form is optional. It has been approved for use in the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL34@P0-1: December 2015 Page 1 F 3003-1.MOTION.BARDATEb. Hearing Set on Regular Notice; Notice Provided Under LBR 9013-1(d): This Motion is set for hearing\nL35@P1: on regular notice pursuant to LBR 9013-1(d). The full Motion and supporting documentation are\nL36@P1: attached, including the legal and factual grounds upon which the Motion is made. If you wish to oppose\nL37@P1: this Motion, you must file a written response with the court and serve it as stated above no later than 14\nL38@P1: days prior to the hearing. Your response must comply with LBR 9013-1(f). The undersigned hereby\nL39@P1: verifies that the hearing date and time selected were available for this type of Motion according to the\nL40@P1: judge’s self-calendaring procedures [LBR 9013-1(b)].\nL41@P1: c. Other (specify):\nL42@P1: Date: _______________ By:\nL43@P1: Signature of Debtor, chapter 11 trustee, or their attorney\nL44@P1: Name:\nL45@P1: Printed name of Debtor, chapter 11 trustee, or their attorney\nL46@P1: This form is optional. It has been approved for use in the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL47@P1-2: December 2015 Page 2 F 3003-1.MOTION.BARDATEMOTION FOR ORDER SETTING BAR DATE FOR FILING PROOFS OF CLAIM\nL48@P2: A party administering a chapter 11 estate must ascertain which creditors assert claims against the estate, and the validity\nL49@P2: of those claims. A proposed form of notice of Bar Date (using mandatory LBR form F 3003-1.NOTICE.BARDATE) is\nL50@P2: attached to this motion as an exhibit.\nL51@P2: The movant requests the court to order as follows, pursuant to FRBP 3003(c)(3):\nL52@P2: 1. 